Upstream-Status: Accepted [https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-build-meta/-/commit/58930ccc3a95bec3a9978c2abf072cd042dd2b0e]
Exit: Drop when the pinned junction's core-deps/systemd-base.bst sets -Dtime-epoch itself.
Subject: core-deps/systemd-base.bst: explicitly set the time epoch

Backport of 58930ccc3a95bec3a9978c2abf072cd042dd2b0e from gnome-build-meta
master (merge request 5222); the gnome-51 branch does not carry it.

The time epoch defaults to SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, which BuildStream sets to
2011-11-11. systemd refuses a clock more than 15 years past its time epoch
and resets it to the epoch, so from 2026-11-11 every boot starts in 2011
until NTP corrects it.

Set the time epoch to the date of the latest git tag, which is what systemd
would use if SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH were not set. The value is a function of the
pinned systemd ref, so it stays reproducible and advances with every bump.

diff --git a/elements/core-deps/systemd-base.bst b/elements/core-deps/systemd-base.bst
--- a/elements/core-deps/systemd-base.bst
+++ b/elements/core-deps/systemd-base.bst
@@ -117,6 +117,7 @@ variables:
     -Dkernel-install=true
     -Dvmlinux-h=provided
     -Dvmlinux-h-path='%{includedir}/%{gcc_triplet}/linux/vmlinux.h'
+    -Dtime-epoch=$(git log --no-show-signature -1 --format=%at $(git describe --abbrev=0 --tags))
 
